# Leak suppressions for cicd/linux/test-sanitizers.bash.
# Only code we don't build goes here, named by the function that leaks, with
# why it's safe to hide. A whole library only where no package of ours ships
# it. The names show only with the debug symbols the lane checks for.
# A leak of ours is fixed. One that has to wait is filed, and the test that
# shows it gets detect_leaks=0 in its meson env, with the backlog ID beside it.
# rkneye51 checks that a leak beside these is still found.

# fontconfig reaches a pattern's entries by an offset from the pattern, not a
# pointer, so the entries of every live pattern look lost. A pattern that is
# really lost still shows, from FcPatternCreate.
leak:FcPatternObjectInsertElt

# GTK 3.24 drops a value each time a CSS transition starts from one still on its
# way: gtk_css_calc_array_add overwrites an entry without its unref. It grows
# with use. Upstream: GNOME's GTK issue tracker, gtk-3-24 branch.
# The function is only on a whole stack, so this matches in rkneye51 alone,
# and the rest of the lane runs with animations off.
leak:gtk_css_value_calc_multiply

# Mesa's GLX setup when GTK opens the display; nothing of ours calls into it,
# and it's the user's own driver.
leak:libGLX_mesa.so.0
